  "notes": "Datasheet SBOS051G covers INA128 and INA129 (identical except gain equation, 50 kΩ vs 49.4 kΩ). The single RG name occupies pins 1 and 8 ('RG 1,8'); split here as RG1/RG8 so each pin appears once - both alias 'RG'. RG pin type printed as '—'; modeled role FEEDBACK, direction BIDIRECTIONAL (passive gain-resistor node). REF->VO and RG1/RG8->VO edges typed SIGNAL_PATH (extractor vocabulary has only POWER_FEED/SIGNAL_PATH for output edges). Many specs are gain-dependent expressions (e.g. VOS '±10 ±100 / G'); stored min/typ/max is the G-independent term and the full expression is in conditions. Spec values differ by grade (P/U vs PA/UA) and by chip site origin (SHE vs FRE); FRE flow only in U (SOIC) packages. PA/UA rows mostly omitted except one VOS row. ± values stored as magnitudes. Output swing values are rail expressions (null). ISC printed as asymmetric '+6/–15' (null). Negative output swing printed in MIN column by x-position (likely should be a max/limit relative to V–). Gain error G = 10 CSO: SHE max printed ±0.4 (wider than FRE ±0.15) - as printed. IQ printed '±700 ±750 µA'."
